WEBVTT

1
00:01:54.281 --> 00:01:56.115
(Wooden swords clacking)

2
00:01:57.159 --> 00:01:59.786
Yah! Left high. left low.

3
00:02:02.664 --> 00:02:05.374
(Swords clanging. men shouting)

4
00:02:17.513 --> 00:02:19.514
Right low. lunge right.

5
00:02:22.810 --> 00:02:25.394
You break anything.
the septa will have my head.

6
00:02:25.521 --> 00:02:27.897
- What is...
- (Screaming)

7
00:02:38.492 --> 00:02:41.035
Your sister knew perfectly well
we were to leave today.

8
00:02:41.161 --> 00:02:43.204
- How she could forget...
- She didn't forget.

9
00:02:43.330 --> 00:02:45.873
She's with her dancing master.
She's with him every morning.

10
00:02:45.999 --> 00:02:48.709
She always comes back with scrapes
and bruises. She's so clumsy.

11
00:02:48.836 --> 00:02:51.045
- Hush!
- (Swords clanging. men yelling)

12
00:02:51.171 --> 00:02:53.673
Go back to your room.

13
00:02:53.799 --> 00:02:57.218
Bar the doors and do not open them
for anyone you do not know.

14
00:02:57.344 --> 00:03:00.263
- What is it? What's happening?
- Do as I told you.

15
00:03:00.389 --> 00:03:02.390
Run!

16
00:03:05.727 --> 00:03:07.645
- (Man) This way!
- (Door banging)

17
00:03:07.771 --> 00:03:10.690
(Screaming)

18
00:03:20.868 --> 00:03:23.578
Left. right. Rah!

19
00:03:23.704 --> 00:03:26.914
- Now you are dead.
- You said right.

20
00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:28.708
but you went left.

21
00:03:28.834 --> 00:03:32.461
- And now you are a dead girl.
- Only 'cause you lied.

22
00:03:32.588 --> 00:03:36.716
My tongue lied.
My eyes shouted the truth.

23
00:03:36.842 --> 00:03:40.094
- You were not seeing.
- I was so. I watched. but you...

24
00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:44.348
Watching is not seeing. dead girl.

25
00:03:46.393 --> 00:03:50.104
The seeing. the true seeing.

26
00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:52.607
that is the heart of swordplay.

27
00:03:52.733 --> 00:03:54.734
(Door opens)

28
00:03:57.070 --> 00:04:00.990
Arya Stark. come with us.
Your father wants to see you.

29
00:04:03.535 --> 00:04:07.288
And why is it that Lord Eddard
is sending Lannister men

30
00:04:07.414 --> 00:04:08.998
in place of his own?

31
00:04:09.124 --> 00:04:12.627
- I am wondering.
- Mind your place. dancing master.

32
00:04:12.753 --> 00:04:16.923
- This is no concern of yours.
- My father wouldn't send you.

33
00:04:20.677 --> 00:04:23.262
And I don't have to go
with you if I don't want.

34
00:04:23.388 --> 00:04:25.640
(Laughs) Take her.

35
00:04:25.766 --> 00:04:29.644
Are you men or snakes.
that you would threaten a child?

36
00:04:29.770 --> 00:04:31.938
Get out of my way. little man.

37
00:04:32.522 --> 00:04:35.274
I am Syrio Forel...

38
00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:37.276
Foreign bastard.

39
00:04:40.155 --> 00:04:43.824
...and you will be speaking to me
with more respect.

40
00:04:43.951 --> 00:04:47.286
Kill the Braavosi. Bring the girl.

41
00:04:47.412 --> 00:04:51.666
Arya child. we are done
with dancing for the day.

42
00:04:51.792 --> 00:04:54.251
Run to your father.

43
00:05:14.147 --> 00:05:15.856
Bloody oafs.

44
00:05:17.317 --> 00:05:21.070
- Begone now. Arya.
- Come with me. Run.

45
00:05:22.823 --> 00:05:25.658
The first sword of Braavos does not run.

46
00:05:36.586 --> 00:05:39.839
- (Wood clatters)
- What do we say

47
00:05:39.965 --> 00:05:42.425
to the god of death?

48
00:05:42.551 --> 00:05:44.260
Not today.

49
00:05:45.846 --> 00:05:48.014
Go.

50
00:05:49.683 --> 00:05:52.351
(Men moaning)

51
00:05:56.231 --> 00:05:59.358
(Swords ringing)
(Men screaming)

52
00:06:12.247 --> 00:06:14.248
Not today. Not today.

53
00:06:17.627 --> 00:06:19.628
(Gasps)

54
00:06:23.925 --> 00:06:27.470
Stay away from me.
I'll tell my father.

55
00:06:28.096 --> 00:06:30.306
I'll... I'll tell the queen.

56
00:06:30.432 --> 00:06:34.018
(Chuckles) Who do you think sent me?

57
00:06:38.065 --> 00:06:40.316
(Horses neighing)

58
00:06:47.115 --> 00:06:49.116
Needle.

59
00:06:51.745 --> 00:06:53.662
There she is.

60
00:06:53.789 --> 00:06:56.082
- What do you want?
- I want you. wolf girl.

61
00:06:56.208 --> 00:06:57.792
- Come here.
- Leave me be.

62
00:06:57.918 --> 00:07:01.587
- My father's a lord. He'll reward you.
- She'll reward me - the queen!

63
00:07:02.339 --> 00:07:04.256
- Stay away!
- (Gasps)

64
00:07:14.643 --> 00:07:17.061
(Door clanging. creaking)

65
00:07:32.869 --> 00:07:36.288
Lord Stark. you must be thirsty.

66
00:07:38.875 --> 00:07:39.959
Varys.

67
00:07:42.003 --> 00:07:44.213
I promise you it isn't poisoned.

68
00:07:45.757 --> 00:07:48.425
Why is it no one ever trusts the eunuch?

69
00:07:56.476 --> 00:07:58.352
Not so much. my lord.

70
00:07:58.478 --> 00:08:00.646
I would save the rest. if I were you.

71
00:08:00.772 --> 00:08:04.608
Hide it. Men have been known
to die of thirst in these cells.

72
00:08:06.319 --> 00:08:08.654
What about my daughters?

73
00:08:08.780 --> 00:08:11.157
The younger one seems
to have escaped the castle.

74
00:08:11.283 --> 00:08:13.868
Even my little birds cannot find her.

75
00:08:13.994 --> 00:08:17.204
- And Sansa?
- Still engaged to Joffrey.

76
00:08:17.330 --> 00:08:21.208
Cersei will keep her close.
The rest of your household though...

77
00:08:21.334 --> 00:08:25.171
all dead. it grieves me to say.
I do so hate the sight of blood.

78
00:08:26.673 --> 00:08:29.675
You watched my men
being slaughtered and did nothing.

79
00:08:29.801 --> 00:08:32.094
And would again. my lord.

80
00:08:32.220 --> 00:08:36.390
I was unarmed. unarmored
and surrounded by Lannister swords.

81
00:08:36.516 --> 00:08:39.643
When you look at me
do you see a hero?

82
00:08:44.900 --> 00:08:47.193
What madness led you to tell the queen

83
00:08:47.319 --> 00:08:50.821
you had learned the truth
about Joffrey's birth?

84
00:08:52.157 --> 00:08:54.158
The madness of mercy.

85
00:08:56.953 --> 00:09:00.581
- That she might save her children.
- Ah. the children.

86
00:09:00.707 --> 00:09:03.918
It's always
the innocents who suffer.

87
00:09:04.044 --> 00:09:07.087
It wasn't the wine
that killed Robert. nor the boar.

88
00:09:07.214 --> 00:09:10.549
The wine slowed him down
and the boar ripped him open.

89
00:09:10.675 --> 00:09:14.053
but it was your mercy
that killed the king.

90
00:09:17.182 --> 00:09:20.809
I trust you know you're
a dead man. Lord Eddard?

91
00:09:24.940 --> 00:09:29.693
The queen can't kill me.
Cat holds her brother.

92
00:09:29.819 --> 00:09:34.323
The wrong brother. sadly.
And lost to her.

93
00:09:34.449 --> 00:09:37.326
Your wife has let the Imp
slip through her fingers.

94
00:09:41.498 --> 00:09:43.707
If that's true.

95
00:09:44.834 --> 00:09:47.878
then slit my throat
and be done with it.

96
00:09:48.004 --> 00:09:50.005
Not today. my lord.

97
00:09:52.926 --> 00:09:55.761
Tell me something. Varys.

98
00:09:56.596 --> 00:09:58.597
Who do you truly serve?

99
00:09:59.933 --> 00:10:02.518
The realm. my lord.

100
00:10:02.644 --> 00:10:04.645
Someone must.

101
00:10:12.779 --> 00:10:14.446
(Door creaks. clangs)

102
00:10:23.623 --> 00:10:26.625
It's Othor. without a doubt.

103
00:10:27.460 --> 00:10:32.172
The other one is Jafer Flowers. my lord.
less the hand the wolf tore off.

104
00:10:32.299 --> 00:10:35.718
Any sign of Benjen
or the rest of his party?

105
00:10:35.844 --> 00:10:39.805
Just these two. my lord.
Been dead awhile. I'd say.

106
00:10:39.931 --> 00:10:42.599
- Mmm.
- The smell.

107
00:10:44.436 --> 00:10:46.645
(Sniffs) What smell?

108
00:10:48.857 --> 00:10:50.691
There is none.

109
00:10:50.817 --> 00:10:54.486
If they'd been dead for a long time.
wouldn't there be rot?

110
00:10:55.905 --> 00:10:59.491
- We should burn them.
- Snow's not wrong. my lord.

111
00:10:59.617 --> 00:11:01.869
Fire will do for them.
The wildling way.

112
00:11:02.662 --> 00:11:05.456
I want Maester Aemon
to examine them first.

113
00:11:06.458 --> 00:11:10.669
You may be a coward. Tarly.
but you're not stupid.

114
00:11:11.254 --> 00:11:14.631
- Get them inside.
- You heard him.

115
00:11:16.301 --> 00:11:17.968
Lord Commander.

116
00:11:19.012 --> 00:11:21.805
Maester Aemon
awaits you in his chambers...

117
00:11:21.931 --> 00:11:24.683
A raven from King's Landing.

118
00:11:25.268 --> 00:11:27.269
Come on. move 'em out.

119
00:11:38.698 --> 00:11:40.699
Bring me a horn of ale. Snow.

120
00:11:41.701 --> 00:11:43.994
and pour one for yourself.

121
00:11:53.922 --> 00:11:56.382
The king is dead.

122
00:12:08.728 --> 00:12:11.021
Is there any word of my father?

123
00:12:11.147 --> 00:12:13.148
Sit.

124
00:12:17.987 --> 00:12:20.406
Lord Stark has been

125
00:12:20.532 --> 00:12:22.241
charged with treason.

126
00:12:23.284 --> 00:12:26.120
They say he conspired
with Robert's brothers

127
00:12:26.246 --> 00:12:29.164
to deny the throne to Prince Joffrey.

128
00:12:40.802 --> 00:12:44.221
I hope you're not thinking
of doing anything stupid.

129
00:12:44.347 --> 00:12:47.766
Your duty lies here now.

130
00:12:48.226 --> 00:12:50.727
My sisters were in King's Landing too.

131
00:12:53.273 --> 00:12:55.232
I'm sure they'll be

132
00:12:55.358 --> 00:12:57.025
treated gently.

133
00:13:00.280 --> 00:13:04.032
(Varys) Your father has proved to be
an awful traitor. dear.

134
00:13:04.159 --> 00:13:07.035
King Robert's body was still warm

135
00:13:07.162 --> 00:13:11.248
when Lord Eddard began plotting
to steal Joffrey's rightful throne.

136
00:13:12.250 --> 00:13:13.834
He wouldn't do that.

137
00:13:13.960 --> 00:13:16.628
He knows how much
I love Joffrey. He wouldn't.

138
00:13:17.672 --> 00:13:19.673
Please. Your Grace.
there's been a mistake.

139
00:13:19.799 --> 00:13:23.343
Send for my father. He'll tell you -
the king was his friend.

140
00:13:23.470 --> 00:13:27.347
Sansa sweetling. you are innocent
of any wrong. We know that.

141
00:13:27.474 --> 00:13:29.933
Yet you are the daughter of a traitor.

142
00:13:30.059 --> 00:13:32.311
How can I allow you to marry my son?

143
00:13:33.062 --> 00:13:35.314
(Pycelle) A child born of a traitor's seed

144
00:13:35.440 --> 00:13:37.733
is no fit consort for our king.

145
00:13:37.859 --> 00:13:40.319
She is a sweet thing now. Your Grace.

146
00:13:40.445 --> 00:13:44.865
but in 10 years who knows
what treasons she may hatch?

147
00:13:44.991 --> 00:13:47.993
No. I'm not. I'll be
a good wife to him. you'll see.

148
00:13:48.119 --> 00:13:52.498
I'll be a queen just like you. I promise.
I won't hatch anything.

149
00:13:54.167 --> 00:13:56.210
The girl is innocent. Your Grace.

150
00:13:57.086 --> 00:14:00.339
She should be given a chance
to prove her loyalty.

151
00:14:03.885 --> 00:14:05.135
(Sighs)

152
00:14:06.846 --> 00:14:11.016
Little dove. you must write to Lady Catelyn
and your brother. the eldest.

153
00:14:11.142 --> 00:14:13.727
- what's his name?
- Robb.

154
00:14:13.853 --> 00:14:16.980
Word of your father's arrest
will reach him soon. no doubt.

155
00:14:17.106 --> 00:14:21.235
Best it comes from you.
If you would help your father.

156
00:14:21.361 --> 00:14:24.571
urge your brother
to keep the king's peace.

157
00:14:24.697 --> 00:14:27.741
Tell him to come to King's Landing
and swear his fealty to Joffrey.

158
00:14:33.081 --> 00:14:38.043
If... If I could see my father.
talk to him about...

159
00:14:40.046 --> 00:14:42.047
You disappoint me. child.

160
00:14:43.550 --> 00:14:45.551
We have told you
of your father's treason.

161
00:14:45.677 --> 00:14:47.886
Why would you want
to speak to a traitor?

162
00:14:48.888 --> 00:14:50.889
I only meant that...

163
00:14:52.392 --> 00:14:54.226
What will happen to him?

164
00:14:55.895 --> 00:14:58.230
- That depends.
- On...

165
00:14:59.232 --> 00:15:01.900
- On what?
- On your brother.

166
00:15:04.904 --> 00:15:06.905
And on you.

167
00:15:15.290 --> 00:15:17.040
Treason?

168
00:15:18.251 --> 00:15:19.626
Sansa wrote this?

169
00:15:19.752 --> 00:15:22.129
It is your sister's hand.
but the queen's words.

170
00:15:22.255 --> 00:15:26.258
You are summoned to King's Landing
to swear fealty to the new king.

171
00:15:26.384 --> 00:15:29.428
Joffrey puts my father in chains.
now he wants his arse kissed?

172
00:15:30.763 --> 00:15:33.432
This is a royal command. my lord.

173
00:15:33.558 --> 00:15:37.227
- If you should refuse to obey...
- I won't refuse.

174
00:15:37.353 --> 00:15:41.356
His Grace summons me to King's Landing.
I'll go to King's Landing.

175
00:15:42.692 --> 00:15:44.359
But not alone.

176
00:15:46.571 --> 00:15:48.196
Call the banners.

177
00:15:49.991 --> 00:15:51.658
All of them. my lord?

178
00:15:51.784 --> 00:15:53.660
They've all sworn to defend my father.
have they not?

179
00:15:53.786 --> 00:15:55.621
They have.

180
00:15:55.747 --> 00:15:57.873
Now we see
what their words are worth.

181
00:16:00.126 --> 00:16:01.126
Yes.

182
00:16:09.761 --> 00:16:11.762
Are you afraid?

183
00:16:14.891 --> 00:16:16.642
I must be.

184
00:16:16.768 --> 00:16:18.185
Good.

185
00:16:19.187 --> 00:16:22.898
- Why is that good?
- It means you're not stupid.

186
00:16:25.860 --> 00:16:27.861
(Cawing)

187
00:16:46.506 --> 00:16:48.173
You've had this since dawn?

188
00:16:49.467 --> 00:16:51.677
He sent it to me. not you.

189
00:16:52.679 --> 00:16:56.014
- I've only shown it to you as a courtesy.
- A courtesy?!

190
00:16:56.140 --> 00:16:58.225
My husband has been taken prisoner.

191
00:16:58.351 --> 00:17:01.728
- My son intends to declare war.
- A war?

192
00:17:01.854 --> 00:17:04.189
Your son against the Lannisters?

193
00:17:05.400 --> 00:17:08.735
You should go to him.
Teach him patience.

194
00:17:08.861 --> 00:17:11.988
Ned rots in a dungeon
and you speak of patience?

195
00:17:12.615 --> 00:17:14.658
He is your brother by law!

196
00:17:14.784 --> 00:17:17.703
Does family mean nothing to you?

197
00:17:17.829 --> 00:17:20.622
Family means everything to me.

198
00:17:20.748 --> 00:17:22.457
And I will not risk Robin's life

199
00:17:22.583 --> 00:17:25.252
to get caught up in another
of your husband's wars.

200
00:17:25.378 --> 00:17:28.588
- I'm hungry.
- Hush now. darling.

201
00:17:28.715 --> 00:17:30.507
You just ate.

202
00:17:30.633 --> 00:17:33.427
You will not support us. then?
Do I understand you correctly?

203
00:17:33.553 --> 00:17:37.222
- But I'm hungry!
- Soon. love. soon.

204
00:17:39.308 --> 00:17:41.393
You're always welcome here. sister.

205
00:17:41.936 --> 00:17:44.688
But if you're asking me
to send men from the Vale to fight...

206
00:17:44.814 --> 00:17:46.898
That is what I ask.

207
00:17:48.943 --> 00:17:50.861
Go on. sweet.

208
00:17:50.987 --> 00:17:52.988
Time for your bath.

209
00:17:53.114 --> 00:17:55.532
I'll feed you after.

210
00:17:59.746 --> 00:18:02.122
If you fear for the safety of your son...

211
00:18:02.248 --> 00:18:05.208
Of course I fear
for the safety of my son!

212
00:18:05.334 --> 00:18:07.252
Are you an idiot?

213
00:18:07.378 --> 00:18:09.796
They killed my husband.

214
00:18:09.922 --> 00:18:12.257
You say they shoved
your boy from a window.

215
00:18:12.383 --> 00:18:16.887
- These people will do anything.
- And that is why we have to stop them.

216
00:18:20.933 --> 00:18:23.477
The knights of the Vale
will stay in the Vale

217
00:18:23.603 --> 00:18:25.187
where they belong.

218
00:18:25.313 --> 00:18:27.481
to protect their lord.

219
00:18:32.236 --> 00:18:35.655
(Tyrion whistling a tune)

220
00:18:40.745 --> 00:18:43.079
Will you shut up?

221
00:18:45.958 --> 00:18:48.126
There's hill tribes all around here.

222
00:18:49.128 --> 00:18:53.089
If I'm going to die. it may as well be
with a song in my heart.

223
00:18:54.091 --> 00:18:56.551
I should just take your food
and leave you here.

224
00:18:56.677 --> 00:18:58.261
Eh?

225
00:18:58.387 --> 00:19:02.349
- What would you do then?
- Starve. most likely.

226
00:19:02.475 --> 00:19:05.060
You don't think I'd do it. do you?

227
00:19:06.020 --> 00:19:09.648
What do you want. Bronn?
Gold? Women?

228
00:19:09.774 --> 00:19:11.775
Golden women?

229
00:19:11.901 --> 00:19:14.069
Stick with me and you'll have them all.

230
00:19:14.195 --> 00:19:17.239
for as long as I'm around
and not a moment longer.

231
00:19:18.241 --> 00:19:20.200
But you knew that.

232
00:19:20.326 --> 00:19:24.287
That is why you so valiantly
took up arms to defend my honor.

233
00:19:25.998 --> 00:19:27.541
Fair enough.

234
00:19:28.417 --> 00:19:30.544
But don't go looking
for me to bend the knee

235
00:19:30.670 --> 00:19:33.880
and "my lord" you
every time you take a shit.

236
00:19:34.006 --> 00:19:37.467
I'm not your toady
and I'm not your friend.

237
00:19:37.593 --> 00:19:39.803
Though I would treasure
your friendship.

238
00:19:39.929 --> 00:19:43.098
I'm mainly interested
in your facility with murder.

239
00:19:43.224 --> 00:19:45.892
And if the day ever comes
when you're tempted to sell me out.

240
00:19:46.018 --> 00:19:47.561
remember this -

241
00:19:47.687 --> 00:19:49.312
whatever their price.

242
00:19:49.438 --> 00:19:51.022
I'll beat it.

243
00:19:51.148 --> 00:19:53.191
I like living.

244
00:19:53.317 --> 00:19:55.110
(Whistles)

245
00:19:57.572 --> 00:20:01.032
- (Rustling)
- (Bronn whispers) Tyrion.

246
00:20:02.785 --> 00:20:10.375
Tyrion.

247
00:20:10.501 --> 00:20:12.210
(Birds chirp. flutter)

248
00:20:31.898 --> 00:20:34.190
Come. share our fire.

249
00:20:35.192 --> 00:20:37.527
Help yourselves to our goat.

250
00:20:44.118 --> 00:20:46.119
When you meet your gods.
