501
00:41:09.801 --> 00:41:12.511
and then it's on
to the Red Keep to free Ned.

502
00:41:13.179 --> 00:41:15.347
- You old devil. Rodrik.
- Jon.

503
00:41:15.473 --> 00:41:17.683
You're not wasting away. are you?

504
00:41:29.279 --> 00:41:32.197
I remember the day
you came into this world.

505
00:41:32.323 --> 00:41:34.825
red-faced and squalling.

506
00:41:36.411 --> 00:41:39.079
And now I find you leading a host to war.

507
00:41:40.206 --> 00:41:42.958
- There was no one else.
- No one?

508
00:41:43.084 --> 00:41:45.127
Who were those men I saw here?

509
00:41:45.253 --> 00:41:49.298
- None of them are Starks.
- All of them are seasoned in battle.

510
00:41:49.424 --> 00:41:51.550
If you think you can
send me back to Winterfell...

511
00:41:51.676 --> 00:41:54.011
Oh. would that I could.

512
00:41:56.890 --> 00:41:59.308
There was...

513
00:41:59.434 --> 00:42:01.435
a letter.

514
00:42:03.730 --> 00:42:06.064
From Sansa.

515
00:42:06.191 --> 00:42:08.358
From the queen. you mean.

516
00:42:16.534 --> 00:42:19.536
- There's no mention of Arya.
- No.

517
00:42:30.173 --> 00:42:32.925
How many men do you have?

518
00:42:33.051 --> 00:42:34.968
18.000.

519
00:42:35.094 --> 00:42:37.429
If I go to King's Landing
and bend my knee to Joffrey...

520
00:42:37.555 --> 00:42:40.432
You would never
be allowed to leave. No.

521
00:42:40.558 --> 00:42:44.269
Our best hope.
our only hope.

522
00:42:44.395 --> 00:42:48.690
- is that you can defeat them in the field.
- And if I lose?

523
00:42:48.816 --> 00:42:51.318
Do you know what happened
to the Targaryen children

524
00:42:51.444 --> 00:42:54.655
- when the Mad King fell?
- They were butchered in their sleep.

525
00:42:54.781 --> 00:42:57.074
On the orders of Tywin Lannister.

526
00:42:57.200 --> 00:42:59.701
And the years have not made him kinder.

527
00:43:03.081 --> 00:43:05.249
If you lose.

528
00:43:05.375 --> 00:43:09.336
your father dies. your sisters die.

529
00:43:09.462 --> 00:43:11.505
we die.

530
00:43:14.592 --> 00:43:16.969
Well. that makes it simple. then.

531
00:43:17.971 --> 00:43:19.471
I suppose it does.

532
00:43:42.704 --> 00:43:46.164
From here it might be best
if Bronn and I continue alone.

533
00:43:46.291 --> 00:43:48.625
Best for Tyrion. son of Tywin.

534
00:43:48.751 --> 00:43:50.502
Not best for me.

535
00:43:51.587 --> 00:43:53.672
If the halfman betrays us.

536
00:43:53.798 --> 00:43:57.551
Shagga. son of Dolf.
will cut off his manhood...

537
00:43:57.677 --> 00:44:00.429
And feed it to the goats. yes.

538
00:44:02.307 --> 00:44:04.808
All right. then.

539
00:44:04.934 --> 00:44:06.935
Time to meet my father.

540
00:44:39.677 --> 00:44:42.012
- Tyrion.
- Uncle.

541
00:44:42.138 --> 00:44:43.972
Father.

542
00:44:45.683 --> 00:44:48.602
The rumors of your demise
were unfounded.

543
00:44:49.771 --> 00:44:52.022
Sorry to disappoint you.

544
00:44:52.857 --> 00:44:54.441
And who are these...

545
00:44:54.567 --> 00:44:56.693
companions of yours?

546
00:44:58.696 --> 00:45:01.740
This is Shagga. son of Dolf.

547
00:45:01.866 --> 00:45:03.867
chieftain of the Stone Crows.

548
00:45:04.327 --> 00:45:08.330
Timett. son of Timett.
ruler of the Burned Men.

549
00:45:08.831 --> 00:45:13.251
This fair maid is Chella.
daughter of Cheyk.

550
00:45:13.378 --> 00:45:15.295
leader of the Black Ears.

551
00:45:15.421 --> 00:45:17.839
And here we have Bronn. son of...

552
00:45:20.009 --> 00:45:22.052
You wouldn't know him.

553
00:45:23.554 --> 00:45:26.014
May I present my lord father.

554
00:45:26.140 --> 00:45:28.767
Tywin. son of Tytos of House Lannister.

555
00:45:28.893 --> 00:45:32.104
Lord of Casterly Rock
and Warden of the West?

556
00:45:33.815 --> 00:45:36.233
Kind of you to go to war for me.

557
00:45:39.195 --> 00:45:41.113
You left us no choice.

558
00:45:41.239 --> 00:45:43.573
The honor of the house was at stake.

559
00:45:44.575 --> 00:45:48.036
Your brother would never have
submitted to capture so meekly.

560
00:45:48.162 --> 00:45:50.580
We have our differences. Jaime and I.

561
00:45:50.706 --> 00:45:52.791
He's braver. I'm better-looking.

562
00:45:52.917 --> 00:45:55.419
He's been covering himself in glory.

563
00:45:55.545 --> 00:45:58.255
Jaime smashed the river lords
at the Golden Tooth.

564
00:45:58.381 --> 00:46:02.259
and now lays siege to Riverrun.
Catelyn Stark's homeland.

565
00:46:02.385 --> 00:46:05.303
- And the Starks? Lord Eddard?
- Is our hostage.

566
00:46:05.763 --> 00:46:08.390
He will lead no armies
from his dungeon cell.

567
00:46:08.516 --> 00:46:12.394
How did my sweet sister persuade the king
to imprison his dear friend Ned?

568
00:46:12.520 --> 00:46:17.274
Robert Baratheon is dead.
Joffrey rules in King's Landing.

569
00:46:19.735 --> 00:46:22.028
My sister rules. you mean.

570
00:46:22.155 --> 00:46:24.239
Stark's son has called his banners.

571
00:46:24.782 --> 00:46:28.702
- He moves south with a strong host.
- A green boy.

572
00:46:28.828 --> 00:46:32.622
One taste of battle and he'll run back
to Winterfell with his tail between his legs.

573
00:46:33.958 --> 00:46:38.378
Maybe. Though the boy does have
a certain belligerence.

574
00:46:38.504 --> 00:46:40.172
You'd like him.

575
00:46:41.215 --> 00:46:45.218
While we're on the subject of war.

576
00:46:45.344 --> 00:46:47.345
I made promises to my friends here.

577
00:46:47.472 --> 00:46:49.848
and a Lannister always pays his debts.

578
00:46:49.974 --> 00:46:52.851
We shall require
3.000 helms and shields.

579
00:46:52.977 --> 00:46:55.061
plus swords. pikes.

580
00:46:55.188 --> 00:46:57.022
gorgets. maces...

581
00:46:57.982 --> 00:47:00.358
If it please my lord.
Ser Addam bids me report

582
00:47:00.485 --> 00:47:02.986
that the northmen
have crossed the Neck.

583
00:47:05.114 --> 00:47:08.742
The wolf rushes
into the lion's jaws. So be it.

584
00:47:08.868 --> 00:47:12.037
Kevan. command
the drummers beat assembly.

585
00:47:13.498 --> 00:47:16.458
And send word to Jaime
that I am moving against Robb Stark.

586
00:47:16.584 --> 00:47:18.460
At once. my lord.

587
00:47:31.182 --> 00:47:34.309
It is said that the men
of the mountain clans are great warriors.

588
00:47:34.435 --> 00:47:36.186
Ride with me against my enemies

589
00:47:36.312 --> 00:47:39.105
and you shall have
all my son promised you and more.

590
00:47:39.232 --> 00:47:41.525
Only if the halfman fights with us.

591
00:47:41.651 --> 00:47:44.319
Until we hold the steel he pledged us.

592
00:47:45.029 --> 00:47:47.864
the little lion's life is ours.

593
00:47:53.204 --> 00:47:56.164
(Rodrik) The scouts report
Lord Tywin moves north.

594
00:47:56.290 --> 00:47:59.209
We need to get him on broken ground.
put his knights at a disadvantage.

595
00:47:59.335 --> 00:48:04.297
No. we need to get around him and break
Jaime Lannister's siege of Riverrun.

596
00:48:04.423 --> 00:48:07.217
Do that and the river lords will join us.

597
00:48:07.343 --> 00:48:10.929
To do either we need to cross the river
and the only crossing is at the Twins.

598
00:48:11.055 --> 00:48:14.432
Lord Frey controls that bridge.
Your father's bannerman.

599
00:48:14.559 --> 00:48:17.769
"The late Lord Frey" my father calls him.

600
00:48:17.895 --> 00:48:21.648
At the Trident. he didn't appear
until the battle was done.

601
00:48:21.774 --> 00:48:25.694
Some men take their oaths
more seriously than others.

602
00:48:27.363 --> 00:48:29.781
(Grunting)

603
00:48:32.827 --> 00:48:35.453
Robb's right.
We need that bridge.

604
00:48:35.580 --> 00:48:37.622
So what's it going to be?

605
00:48:37.748 --> 00:48:41.501
Do we move against
Jaime or Lord Tywin?

606
00:48:45.715 --> 00:48:49.384
Your pardon. my lords.
We've captured a Lannister scout.

607
00:48:51.345 --> 00:48:54.598
Don't worry. lad. He won't be
leaving this tent with his head.

608
00:48:56.100 --> 00:48:59.853
- Where did you find him?
- In the brush above the encampment.

609
00:48:59.979 --> 00:49:02.147
He looked to be counting.

610
00:49:12.283 --> 00:49:13.908
How high did you get?

611
00:49:16.412 --> 00:49:19.164
20.000. Maybe more.

612
00:49:19.290 --> 00:49:22.709
You don't have to do this yourself.
Your father would understand...

613
00:49:22.835 --> 00:49:26.796
My father understands mercy.
when there is room for it.

614
00:49:28.716 --> 00:49:31.468
And he understands honor...

615
00:49:32.845 --> 00:49:35.096
and courage.

616
00:49:37.183 --> 00:49:39.351
Let him go.

617
00:49:39.894 --> 00:49:42.145
Robb.

618
00:49:54.325 --> 00:49:57.661
Tell Lord Tywin
winter is coming for him.

619
00:49:57.787 --> 00:50:02.165
20.000 northerners marching south
to find out if he really does shit gold.

620
00:50:04.293 --> 00:50:06.544
Yes. my lord.

621
00:50:06.671 --> 00:50:08.672
Thank you. my lord.

622
00:50:17.223 --> 00:50:20.892
Are you touched. boy?!
Letting him go?

623
00:50:21.018 --> 00:50:22.686
You call me boy again.

624
00:50:24.355 --> 00:50:25.855
Go on.

625
00:50:35.157 --> 00:50:37.325
(Growls)

626
00:50:43.457 --> 00:50:45.458
Oi.

627
00:50:51.382 --> 00:50:54.259
(Pycelle) It is also the wish of His Grace

628
00:50:54.385 --> 00:50:58.304
that his loyal servant Janos Slynt.

629
00:50:59.515 --> 00:51:02.183
- Commander of the City Watch...
- Ser Aron.

630
00:51:02.309 --> 00:51:06.938
...be at once raised to the rank of lord...

631
00:51:07.064 --> 00:51:08.356
Lord Gyles.

632
00:51:08.482 --> 00:51:11.776
...and granted
the ancient seat of Harrenhal.

633
00:51:11.902 --> 00:51:15.447
and that his sons and grandsons
shall hold this honor

634
00:51:15.573 --> 00:51:20.452
after him until the end of time.

635
00:51:20.578 --> 00:51:22.954
(Lords mutter)

636
00:51:23.956 --> 00:51:28.001
In the place of the traitor Eddard Stark.

637
00:51:28.127 --> 00:51:32.422
it is the wish of His Grace
that Tywin Lannister.

638
00:51:32.548 --> 00:51:36.968
Lord of Casterly Rock
and Warden of the West.

639
00:51:37.094 --> 00:51:40.305
be appointed Hand of the King.

640
00:51:40.431 --> 00:51:42.348
Lastly.

641
00:51:42.475 --> 00:51:45.226
in these times of treason and turmoil.

642
00:51:45.352 --> 00:51:48.396
it is the view of council

643
00:51:48.522 --> 00:51:51.566
that the life and safety

644
00:51:51.692 --> 00:51:53.610
of King Joffrey

645
00:51:53.736 --> 00:51:57.864
be of paramount importance.

646
00:51:59.492 --> 00:52:02.035
Ser Barristan Selmy.

647
00:52:08.542 --> 00:52:11.920
Your Grace.
I am yours to command.

648
00:52:12.046 --> 00:52:14.005
Rise. Ser Barristan.

649
00:52:14.924 --> 00:52:16.966
You may remove your helm.

650
00:52:22.139 --> 00:52:24.641
You have served the realm
long and faithfully.

651
00:52:24.767 --> 00:52:28.520
Every man and woman
in the Seven Kingdoms owes you thanks.

652
00:52:28.646 --> 00:52:31.940
But it is time to put aside
your armor and your sword.

653
00:52:32.066 --> 00:52:34.818
It is time to rest
and look back with pride

654
00:52:34.944 --> 00:52:37.821
- on your many years of service.
- (Murmuring)

655
00:52:38.739 --> 00:52:41.199
Your Grace. the Kingsguard
is a sworn brotherhood.

656
00:52:41.325 --> 00:52:45.870
Our vows are taken for life.
Only death relieves us of our sacred trust.

657
00:52:45.996 --> 00:52:49.791
Whose death. Ser Barristan?
Yours or your king's?

658
00:52:50.626 --> 00:52:52.544
(Joffrey) You let my father die.

659
00:52:52.670 --> 00:52:55.463
You're too old to protect anybody.

660
00:52:58.342 --> 00:53:00.468
- Your Grace...
- The council has determined

661
00:53:00.594 --> 00:53:03.054
that Ser Jaime Lannister
will take your place

662
00:53:03.180 --> 00:53:06.891
- as Lord Commander of the Kingsguard.
- The man who profaned his blade

663
00:53:07.017 --> 00:53:09.060
with the blood of the king
he had sworn to defend!

664
00:53:09.186 --> 00:53:11.062
Careful. ser.

665
00:53:11.188 --> 00:53:15.275
We have nothing but gratitude
for your long service. good ser.

666
00:53:15.401 --> 00:53:17.902
You shall be given
a stout keep beside the sea.

667
00:53:18.028 --> 00:53:20.738
with servants
to look after your every need.

668
00:53:20.865 --> 00:53:24.826
A hall to die in
and men to bury me.

669
00:53:27.037 --> 00:53:29.414
I am a knight.

670
00:53:29.540 --> 00:53:32.542
I shall die a knight.

671
00:53:38.549 --> 00:53:40.592
A naked knight. apparently.

672
00:53:40.718 --> 00:53:42.719
(Laughter)

673
00:53:51.896 --> 00:53:55.690
Even now I could cut through
the five of you like carving a cake!

674
00:53:59.737 --> 00:54:01.946
Here. boy!

675
00:54:02.072 --> 00:54:04.657
Melt it down and add it to the others.

676
00:54:18.923 --> 00:54:20.882
(Doors creak. clang)

677
00:54:21.008 --> 00:54:23.259
If any man in this hall
has other matters

678
00:54:23.385 --> 00:54:27.055
to set before His Grace.
let him speak now

679
00:54:27.181 --> 00:54:29.641
or go forth and hold his silence.

680
00:54:32.895 --> 00:54:34.604
Your Grace.

681
00:54:35.814 --> 00:54:37.815
Come forward. my lady.

682
00:54:38.817 --> 00:54:41.653
(Steward) The Lady Sansa
of House Stark.

683
00:54:42.780 --> 00:54:46.366
Do you have some business
for the king and the council. Sansa?

684
00:54:46.951 --> 00:54:48.409
I do.

685
00:54:53.123 --> 00:54:56.709
As it please Your Grace.
I ask mercy for my father.

686
00:54:56.835 --> 00:54:59.420
Lord Eddard Stark.
who was Hand of the King.

687
00:54:59.546 --> 00:55:02.674
Treason is a noxious weed.

688
00:55:03.342 --> 00:55:06.844
- It should be torn out. root...
- Let her speak.

689
00:55:06.971 --> 00:55:09.639
I want to hear what she says.

690
00:55:09.974 --> 00:55:11.683
Thank you. Your Grace.

691
00:55:11.809 --> 00:55:14.352
Do you deny your father's crime?

692
00:55:14.478 --> 00:55:18.231
No. my lords.
I know he must be punished.

693
00:55:19.233 --> 00:55:20.984
All I ask is mercy.

694
00:55:21.485 --> 00:55:23.736
I know my lord father
must regret what he did.

695
00:55:23.862 --> 00:55:25.863
He was King Robert's friend
and he loved him.

696
00:55:25.990 --> 00:55:27.657
You all know he loved him.

697
00:55:28.492 --> 00:55:32.495
He never wanted to be Hand
until the king asked him.

698
00:55:32.621 --> 00:55:36.374
They must have lied to him -
Lord Renly or Lord Stannis or somebody.

699
00:55:36.500 --> 00:55:38.334
They must have lied!

700
00:55:38.836 --> 00:55:40.837
He said I wasn't the king.

701
00:55:41.714 --> 00:55:45.174
- Why did he say that?
- He was badly hurt.

702
00:55:45.300 --> 00:55:48.261
Maester Pycelle
was giving him milk of the poppy.

703
00:55:48.387 --> 00:55:52.181
He wasn't himself.
Otherwise he never would have said it.

704
00:55:54.184 --> 00:55:56.227
A child's faith.

705
00:55:56.353 --> 00:55:58.646
Such sweet innocence.

706
00:55:59.314 --> 00:56:03.526
And yet they say wisdom
oft comes from the mouths of babes.

707
00:56:04.028 --> 00:56:08.156
Treason is treason!

708
00:56:11.410 --> 00:56:13.494
Anything else?

709
00:56:15.039 --> 00:56:18.791
If you still have any affection
in your heart for me.

710
00:56:18.917 --> 00:56:22.045
please do me this kindness. Your Grace.

711
00:56:31.722 --> 00:56:33.806
Your sweet words have moved me.

712
00:56:35.934 --> 00:56:38.853
But your father has to confess.

713
00:56:38.979 --> 00:56:42.440
He has to confess
and say that I'm the king...

714
00:56:45.069 --> 00:56:47.445
or there'll be no mercy for him.

715
00:56:52.076 --> 00:56:54.077
He will.
